          "summary": "Give each Party an unrestricted right to exploit and license jointly-owned inventions, removing the internal-use-only limitation and consent requirement.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] Section 11.1(c) creates joint ownership, but 11.1(d) then limits us to internal use of that jointly-owned IP and blocks any licensing without Array's consent. We need an unrestricted right to practise, exploit and license our own co-owned inventions (subject to the exclusive licences already granted), which our playbook treats as the minimum acceptable alternative to no joint ownership at all; we have kept a consent requirement on outright assignment of a co-ownership interest, which protects both Parties.",
